# Frontend Standards

## Code Quality

- Functional components + custom hooks; no duplicate logic
- Reuse `client/src/components/ui/` and existing hooks (`useIssuesFeed`, `useDebounce`, `useInfiniteScroll`)
- Meaningful folder structure; consistent naming; comment only non-obvious business logic
- Type-safe patterns where possible (JSDoc or TS if migrating)

## Performance

Lazy loading, route splitting, code splitting, memoization (`React.memo`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`), image optimization, React Query caching, optimistic updates for support/comment actions.

## Accessibility

Keyboard navigation, ARIA labels, screen reader support, WCAG-compliant contrast using design tokens, focus-visible states on interactive elements.

## State & Data

- React Query for server state; Zustand for client UI state (theme, filters)
- Socket.IO via `SocketContext` — invalidate or patch cache on events
- React Hook Form for report/admin forms; React Hot Toast for feedback

## API Layer

Extend `client/src/services/` and `client/src/api/` — never duplicate fetch logic in components.

```jsx
// ✅ Data in hook, UI in component
const { issues, fetchNextPage, isLoading } = useIssuesFeed(filters);

// ❌ Raw fetch in JSX
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/issues').then(...) }, []);
```
